<article class="env-example" id="09FX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09FX">Example <span data-tag="09FX">9.6.4</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field, and $P \in k[x]$ an irreducible polynomial. We have seen that $k[x]/(P)$ is a field (Example <a href="/tag/09FI" data-tag="09FI">9.3.3</a>). Since it is also a $k$-algebra in the obvious way, it is an extension of $k$. </p>
